herein.Department personnel provided pursuant to this Agreement will be subject to other assignments
in times of emergencies, as determined by the Department.In selecting personnel to provide services
pursuant to this Agreement, the Department shall consider the officer’s interest in the assignment, ability
to deal with the District's students, and any special training which may have been received.
10.Department personnel providing services pursuant to this Agreement shall conduct
themselves as police officers and shall at all times follow the policies and procedures of the Department.
11.The Department shall provide routine police services to the District at the following
locationand at the following times:
a.
One officer stationed at Johnson Junior High School but responsible for calls at
allschools participating in the summer school program.This officer will be
available from 7:30 A.M. to 12:30 P.M.(five (5) hours)per day during the
summer school session, a total of twenty-six (26) days.The Officer assigned to
this location shall perform routine police services during regular summer school
hours.
b.
Officers at athletic events, school dances, and other special events as may be
determined by mutual agreement between the Department and the District,
subject to the availability of Department personnel.
